    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a pretty strong stance to take. if you're saying the pattern of evasion \"strongly favors\" the conclusion of bad faith, aren't you essentially deciding the verdict for the case? it feels like you're dismissing the possibility that a highly trained politician might use that kind of language as a legal safeguard to avoid making unintended legal errors, rather than to lie. if you were writing this for a legal journal, wouldn't you be expected to weight those two interpretations more equally instead of siding with the 'misleading' argument?",
